**The finding.** The receipt refusal is not the one acceptable stub refusal, so it counts as a finding that must be cured before any real plan is armed. The gate in `joulewise/night_gate.py` reads the chain script for every receipt class, while the driver substitutes its built-in stub and never writes that file. The gate refused on the missing file, and the driver then overrode the refusal because the class is a rehearsal. The existing gate test did not catch this because its fake probe source serves chain text. I wrote the root cause, two cure options with a recommendation, and the needed test shape to `night/courier.finding.md` in the custody root for the magistrate to harvest.

**Next lane.** The remaining steps belong to the relaunched magistrate, which the watchdog will spawn once the plan span ends. They include harvesting the records into NIGHT-REHEARSAL-01, uninstalling the two night agents from the stub checkout, removing the stub checkout and plan root, landing the gate cure, and sending Ed the stage-1 plan email. I did not run the uninstall or removal steps. This session runs inside the checkout being removed, and those actions are the magistrate's to take after harvest.
